that runs only that test", "cwd": "."}], "choices": [{"choice": "one sentence", "scope":
"product"|"behavior"|"detail", "reasoning": "...", "requirements": ["req:..."]}]}
supportFiles are build or configuration files required for the run commands to execute (empty array
if none are needed or they already exist). choices lists what you had to invent because no statement
decides it: the choice in one sentence, its scope (product, behavior, or detail), your reasoning,
and the requirements it fills in when any exist; an empty array when you invented nothing.

A run command that cannot execute from a fresh checkout of the deliverable is a defect: if it needs
a runner or build file no listed file provides (a package.json for npx jest, a Cargo.toml for cargo
test), you MUST return that file in supportFiles.
